{"at":"2026-11-13T05:13:38.553Z","round":6,"event":"write","id":"chapter_intro_cards","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7439601,"turns":26,"summary":"I've built the chapter intro cards, but I haven't run them. This session wasn't allowed to run `npm run boot-test` (or even a `node --check` syntax check), so the harness's boot test will be the first time the code runs.\n\n**What I built:** a new file, `src/ui/chapterIntro.js`, exports `showChapterIntro(scene, chapter, onDone)`. It shows a card over the screen with \"CHAPTER N\", the district, the season, and the Calendar's \"typical reasons\" line word for word. I left out the bible's tag notes (like \"so `quick_bite`\") so the card doesn't hint at clues.\n\n**Where it appears:**\n- **Chat** (`src/scenes/ChatScene.js`): the card shows before the first message the first time any level of a chapter opens, then never again automatically. Which chapters have been seen is saved in localStorage, wrapped in try/catch. While the card is up, the chat ignores space, A, P and clicks. Rereading after a miss skips the card.\n- **Menu** (`src/scenes/MenuScene.js`): tapping a chapter heading shows its card again.\n\nThe card closes with a click, Enter or Esc. A click only counts if it starts on the card, so the click that opened it from the menu doesn't close it straight away, and the closing click doesn't also skip a chat message. Animation goes through `tween()`, so with Reduce motion on the card appears at once.\n\nI also added the bullet to the \"Decisions taken in the prototype\" list in `CLAUDE.md`. Files changed: `src/ui/chapterIntro.js` (new), `src/scenes/ChatScene.js`, `src/scenes/MenuScene.js` and `CLAUDE.md`."}
