{"at":"2026-11-13T05:18:13.396Z","round":7,"event":"write","id":"how_to_play","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.9498232,"turns":28,"summary":"I added How to play, but I haven't run anything: `npm run boot-test` and `node --check` both needed approval in this session, so the code hasn't been tested in a browser or syntax-checked.\n\n- **New file `src/ui/howToPlay.js`:** it exports `showHowToPlay(scene, onDone)`, a three-step overlay: read the group chat, check every place, recommend one place. Each step puts a pulsing outline, a label and an arrow on the part of the chat screen it means: the chat panel, the \"Find a place\" button, then the Notebook. It has Next and Skip buttons, Enter goes to the next step and Esc skips. Being seen is remembered in localStorage inside try/catch, and all animation goes through `tween()`.\n- **`src/scenes/ChatScene.js`:** it shows the overlay the first time level 1 opens, before the chapter card, then starts the chat.\n- **`src/scenes/OptionsScene.js`:** it has a \"How to play\" button under the preview (H also opens it). The screen's own keys wait while the overlay is up, so Esc closes the overlay without leaving Options.\n- **`CLAUDE.md`:** it has the new bullet.\n\nThe overlay's step 3 points at the Notebook, since the recommend button is on a different screen. Options shows the same chat-screen outlines, so there they act as a diagram rather than pointing at real controls. The browser boot test will run the overlay on level_01 but doesn't check its contents."}
