{"at":"2026-11-13T19:16:58.847Z","round":3,"event":"write","id":"asset_folders","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.6401091999999998,"turns":26,"summary":"I made the changes, but I couldn't run anything: `npm run boot-test` and `node tools/sync_assets.mjs` were both blocked pending approval. So the boot test and the new sync script are untested and are left for the harness run. `tools/slice_portraits.py` now reads from `assets/art` (`SRC = os.path.join(ROOT, 'assets', 'art')`), and its docstrings use the new path. I added `tools/sync_assets.mjs`, a Node script with no dependencies: it copies every `.mp3`/`.ogg` and `*-license.txt` from `../assets/music/` into `public/music/`, creates the folder, removes files no longer in `assets/music/` and prints what it did. It never changes anything in `assets/`. `package.json` gained `sync-assets` plus `predev`, `prebuild` and `preboot-test`, which all run the sync. The remaining `art/source/` mentions in `src/scenes/OutcomeScene.js` (the image placeholder text), `src/ui/cityMap.js` and `src/ui/theme.js` now say `assets/art/`. In `CLAUDE.md` I changed the Art section paths, added a line saying `game/public/music/` is a generated copy of `assets/music/` (ignored by Git), and added the \"Assets folders\" decision bullet ending \"(feature agent, 2026-11-13)\". `public/music/` was already in `.gitignore`, so I didn't change it."}
